5eab62e5-8d3f-4e40-ae56-cd0a008a645f	d0c9ab98-489b-4f87-be85-03db4b7960f5	f91dabe0-17c1-41ad-aa08-46549c13043f	c27caa9c-e0c7-4819-99fc-304920e73f76	36	Lesson 1	Page 37	efeb3395-230e-49c9-9a8d-d60ab84da23f	36\nTable 3.2 Software requirements needed to ensure compatibility and run\nthe system efficiently and effectively. software, instructions that tell a computer\nwhat to do. Software  comprises the entire set of programs, procedures, and\nroutines associated with the operation of a computer system. Britannica (2026).\nThe system design to ensure compatibility and efficient operation, the\nsystem requires specific software components. At minimum, the operating system\nshould be Windows 11 or Android 10 and above, with the latest stable release\nrecommended for enhanced security and performance. The system must function\nwith internet access required, though a stable mobile data or broadband\nconnection is advisable for smoother data transfer and real-time interactions. The\nprogramming languages used in development include Pyth on, HTML, CSS, and\nJavaScript, and it is recommended to utilize updated versions of these languages\nto maintain compatibility with modern frameworks and libraries. For data\nmanagement, PostgreSQL serves as the database system, providing reliable\nstorage and retrieval of information, and more strict security and structure with the\nlatest stable release recommended to ensure optimal performance and security.\nOverall, these software requirements are essential to guarantee that the system\nruns effectively, supports scalability, and delivers a seamless user experience.\n. The researcher developed a Gantt chart, presented as Figure 3.2, to\nserve as a guide for project implementation. This chart highlighted the key\nmilestones necessary to ensure that tasks were completed within the designated\ntimeframe and that the overall project advanced according to the deadlines set by\nthe researcher.
