e5b90ca0-d81a-4cc6-b56b-c00ba3aa4202	c9f395d3-9f01-439b-a749-2b1b58c239c1	af4ef209-43d9-4f34-8836-d73e090f1409	0	multiple_choice	Which of the following is NOT one of the four fundamental electrical concepts described in the lesson?	[{"id": "1c180568-6af2-42d5-b32f-1815effd2a59", "text": "Current"}, {"id": "2b78bece-dc52-4f76-9d71-7cb6611d91dc", "text": "Voltage"}, {"id": "d4cc5ec1-9c46-42c4-b79f-6d27487633d1", "text": "Capacitance"}, {"id": "d4c44860-1f48-4fd3-ab4f-f14199840341", "text": "Power"}]	"d4cc5ec1-9c46-42c4-b79f-6d27487633d1"	Capacitance is not listed among the four core concepts (current, voltage, resistance, power).	1.00	{"title": "File", "item_id": "9fb31b76-250b-402b-81e5-56d1d2d21dd6", "revision_id": "8591adf5-04e8-4de2-8f24-e4125a7f4df1"}
