b337b982-5a01-4137-ba3c-c5faa0744f93	c9f395d3-9f01-439b-a749-2b1b58c239c1	c759971c-4a34-4b12-8c74-0890a4dbe8bd	2	multiple_choice	Which statement best describes why AC is widely used for power distribution?	[{"id": "d05dcd49-70b6-4d68-a730-ea922be3be44", "text": "AC can be easily converted to DC by a simple resistor"}, {"id": "9155b2c8-ff61-43e5-829a-b2c6e4beba83", "text": "AC allows transformers to step voltage up or down"}, {"id": "93c4db90-84a9-4027-8046-f7c7a4c22c46", "text": "AC does not require any conversion to power electronic devices"}, {"id": "92b67167-f3b5-4c76-b0ba-e2e7217ec115", "text": "AC is the only type of current that can flow in a circuit"}]	"9155b2c8-ff61-43e5-829a-b2c6e4beba83"	Transformers work only with AC, enabling voltage transformation for distribution.	1.00	{"title": "File", "item_id": "9fb31b76-250b-402b-81e5-56d1d2d21dd6", "revision_id": "8591adf5-04e8-4de2-8f24-e4125a7f4df1"}
94fad8c0-ebe7-46c3-802d-d188c5015420	c9f395d3-9f01-439b-a749-2b1b58c239c1	47c56934-60fa-4fc1-9105-38dc8bc907e6	3	true_false	Direct Current (DC) flows in one direction only.	[]	true	DC is defined as current that flows in a single direction.	1.00	{"title": "File", "item_id": "9fb31b76-250b-402b-81e5-56d1d2d21dd6", "revision_id": "8591adf5-04e8-4de2-8f24-e4125a7f4df1"}
